DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260512T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260512T170000
UID:69ebd2e32866a5b4884aa8ee@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join\nTV host and celebrity chef Sang Kim\nfor a hands-on Bibi
 mbap rice bowl making experience made just for teens!\nLearn to make a nut
 ritious rice bowl based on Korean traditions. Ingredients include: a varie
 ty of seasoned vegetables\, cooked egg (optional)\, and spicy-sweet-vinega
 ry sauce.\nLimited spots. Online registration begins May 4. Please arrive 
 by 3:45pm\nFood allergy notice: Please be aware that food will be used in 
 this program.  Certain food ingredients may cause allergic reactions in so
 me people.\nProgram is held in the Youth Hub for\nTEENS ONLY\n.\nThis prog
 ram is part of Youth Hub service. Youth Hubs are a welcoming place for tee
 ns after school and in the summer\, where helpful staff are always availab
 le. Free\, nutritious snacks are offered daily. Drop by a branch with a\
 nYouth Hub\nor call the branch to find out more.\nInformation Collection N
 otice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto 
 Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, a
 nd 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registra
 tion\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles yo
 ur information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n
 \, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Bridlewood\, Youth Hub
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69ebd2e32866a5b4884aa8ee
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
