BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Youth Hub: Dungeons & Dragons
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260604T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260604T180000
UID:69f0e861c1cf6f9a758867d0@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Are you ready for an adventure? Join us in the Youth Hub for o
 ur weekly Dungeons and Dragons game. Delve into a fantasy world to fight m
 onsters and discover lost treasures in forgotten places. New players will
  be taught the rules and basics of play. Participants can either bring the
 ir own 1st level character or use one of our prepared sheets. Game will be
  run using the 2024 edition of Dungeons & Dragons.\nEach adventure is run 
 twice a week\, once on Thursday and once on Friday\; players can register 
 for either Thursday OR Friday\, but not both. Players do not have to atten
 d the same day every week.\nThis is a Youth Hub program for teens. Space i
 s limited\, registration required.\nThis program is part of Youth Hub serv
 ice. Youth Hubs are a welcoming place for teens after school and in the su
 mmer\, where helpful staff are always available. Free\, nutritious snacks
  are offered daily. Drop by a branch with a\nYouth Hub\nor call the branc
 h to find out more.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal informat
 ion on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Publ
 ic Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information wil
 l only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluatio
 n. Questions about how the library handles your information can be directe
 d to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge S
 treet\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Maria A. Shchuka\, Youth Hub
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69f0e861c1cf6f9a758867d0
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
